# Flutter / Dart conventions

- Features live in `lib/features/<name>/`. Domain has no Flutter, Dio, Hive, or Riverpod.
- Data layer maps APIs/cache into models and implements repository interfaces.
- Presentation is pages, widgets, and Riverpod providers only.
- Use `ConsumerWidget` / `ConsumerStatefulWidget`. `ref.watch` in `build`; `ref.read` for actions.
- Cross-boundary errors: `Either<Failure, T>` from `lib/core/utils/failure.dart`.
- User-facing text: add `ar` and `en` keys in `app_localizations.dart`, then `context.tr('key')`.
- Colors and type come from `AppTheme` and `design_colors.dart`.
- Prefer Material 3 widgets (`FilledButton`, `NavigationBar`, `MenuAnchor`, `SegmentedButton`, `Switch.adaptive`).
- Network I/O goes through `SecureHttpClient`. Logging uses `AppLogger`.
- Keep I/O in `lib/core/services` or feature `data/` — not inside `build()`.
- `prayer_times` is the architecture reference. Match it when adding domain/data to other features.
